+  Operator directive 2026-06-13: pre-stage .384 with the corrected accumulation config; letting
+  the planner author .383 cost a milestone. ROOT CAUSE (outer-loop diagnostic 2026-06-13):
+  .383's accumulation passes (exp4135-4138) NO-OP'd. exp4135 ran 6.99s, return_code 0, stdout
+  stopped at "Creating TRM ...", val=null, and the stable checkpoint
+  (results/trm_runs/sudoku_extreme_baseline/last.ckpt) was NEVER updated (still the .382 exp4127
+  checkpoint, ~0.278 val, mtime 00:41). A 7s CLEAN exit on a RESUMED checkpoint = the checkpoint
+  reached the config's `max_epochs` cap, so `trainer.fit()` returned immediately. The planner's
+  command was also missing `ckpt_path=` + `+trainer.max_time=`. The accumulate-floor + config-audit
+  correctly halted the chain (no fake progress), and the graft (exp4139) deferred uninformatively
+  (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK) on the non-faithful 0.278 baseline. So the TRM-verifier question AND the
+  queued DiffusionGemma gate are BOTH still open.
+
+  THE GOOD NEWS: the 0.278 checkpoint is INTACT. .384 resumes from it and just needs the CORRECT
+  command + the max_epochs fix to push 0.278 -> ~0.87.
+
+  THE FIX (exp4146, then 4147-4149): every accumulation pass MUST
+  (1) RESUME: `ckpt_path=results/trm_runs/sudoku_extreme_baseline/last.ckpt`;
+  (2) RAISE THE EPOCH CEILING: read the checkpoint's current epoch (torch.load -> ['epoch'] or the
+      trainer state) and set `+trainer.max_epochs=<current_epoch + a generous budget>` so training
+      CONTINUES instead of instantly returning (THE bug);
+  (3) BOUND THE PASS: `+trainer.max_time="00:01:00:00"` (<=60 min, stops + saves before the 80-min cap);
+  (4) WRITE BACK to the SAME stable dir (so the next pass resumes);
+  (5) ANTI-NO-OP GUARD: assert the pass ACTUALLY trained -- duration_s > 120 AND the checkpoint
+      epoch ADVANCED AND a real val_exact_accuracy was read from the metrics CSV. A <120s run or an
+      unchanged epoch = `blocked_noop_<reason>`, NOT `complete`.
+
+  Mirror the WORKING exp4116/exp4127 mechanics (those reached 0.278); the only additions are the
+  max_epochs-ceiling raise + the anti-no-op guard. ACCUMULATE FLOOR still applies: if val does not
+  advance across a real (non-no-op) pass, flag a deeper config audit. If .384 ends < 0.87, .385
+  continues from the stable checkpoint.
+
+  THEN exp4150 (THE DECISIVE GRAFT, defensive): only if val >= 0.85 (faithful) run the Carnot Sudoku
+  verifier graft (rerank + A=verifier-cert vs B=vote-cert de-confound) -- THE result that resolves
+  both the moat question and the DiffusionGemma gate. Else defer honestly; .385 continues.
 
